menu "Board configuration"

choice
    prompt "Target board type"
    default BOARD_TYPE_SMD4
    help
        Select the pin map for the hardware variant. All supported boards
        use the ES8388 codec.

config BOARD_TYPE_SMD2
    bool "SMD2 gateway (ES8388, ESP32-C6-WROOM-1 pin map)"

config BOARD_TYPE_SMD4
    bool "SMD4 gateway (ES8388, ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 pin map)"
    help
        Analog Redial v4, the current board -- see docs/hardware-smd4.md
        and archive/hardware/smd4.md. A different GPIO map from SMD2: the
        MCU is an ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 carrier rather than a soldered
        WROOM-1 module.

config BOARD_TYPE_SMD5
    bool "SMD5 gateway, real Espressif module (ES8388, ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 pin map, native USB)"
    help
        Analog Redial v5 -- see archive/hardware/smd5.md. Same pin map as
        SMD4, plus the BM64 companion's MFB on GPIO15. Use this for either
        MCU module as long as the JP2/JP3 jumpers match the module.

config BOARD_TYPE_SMD5_CHEAP
    bool "SMD5 gateway, AliExpress clone module (ES8388, ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 pin map, no native USB)"
    help
        Only for an SMD5 with the clone module whose JP2/JP3 jumpers were
        left at the default: MCLK and card-detect then land on the clone's
        GPIO12/13 (its native USB pins), so this build remaps them, detaches
        the USB PHY, and puts the console on UART0 (sdkconfig.smd5_cheap
        .defaults). See archive/hardware/smd5.md.

endchoice

endmenu
